Incremental Find Object
Clicking the button and starting to type the name of the object you want to find finds and highlights that
object in the opened Frame window.
Remarks
Microsoft describes Incremental Find Object as "a type of search that looks for a string in an automatic
and progressive way. As the user types a string, possible matches are found, thus enabling the user to stop
typing the complete string as soon as the right match is found."
Plant Simulation shows the characters you type in the status bar 
 . You can type all
characters which are allowed for object names. As we do not distinguish upper- or lower-casing in object
names, you can start typing with lower-case letters.
As soon as Plant Simulation finds an object that matches these characters, it selects that object and zooms
to it in the 3D scene. If you want to return to the last active scene before the search, press Backspace.
If Incremental Find Object did not find and select the object you wanted to find, it returns to the scene as
it was before you started searching.
You can use these keys to control the functionality of Incremental Find Object:
• Press Backspace to delete the last character you typed. Then, type in the correct character.
• Press Tab to find the next matching object of the characters you typed. If no additional object is found,
Plant Simulation selects the first object you wanted to find again and shows it. It also plays a signal tone.
When cycling through the object that match the search, Plant Simulation shows the names of the
objects in the status bar instead of the search pattern.
• Press Esc to terminate Incremental Find Object. Plant Simulation retains the current selection of the
object it found.
• Press Return to terminate Incremental Find Object and execute the default operation of Return for the
object, for example open the simulation properties dialog.
Note
To find the name of an object in an open folder in the Class Library, press Ctrl+I and start typing.
Incremental Find Object
Plant Simulation Help 11-1429
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

